vLLM 0.32.0: return llama.cpp-compatible `timings` in chat responses

llama-swap derives the model dashboard's Prefill/Decode from the response body's
`timings` object (prompt_per_second / predicted_per_second), the same block
llama-server emits. vLLM's response has only `usage`, so the panel stayed empty.

Adds an optional `timings` field to ChatCompletionResponse and
ChatCompletionStreamResponse (final chunk) and fills it from RequestStateStats.

Apply from site-packages: patch -p1 < this-file
Revert:                  patch -R -p1 < this-file

--- a/vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py
@@ -140,6 +140,8 @@
     service_tier: Literal["auto", "default", "flex", "scale", "priority"] | None = None
     system_fingerprint: str | None = None
     usage: UsageInfo
